            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:6",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "He slew of Edom in the valley of salt ten thousand, and took Selah by war, and called the name of it Joktheel unto this day.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "2 Sam. 8:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Sam. 8:13.",
            "prettyString": "2 Samuel 8:13",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2samuel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 8,
                    "end": 8,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 13,
                        "end": 13
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:7",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Amaziah sent messengers to Jehoash, the son of Jehoahaz son of Jehu, king of Israel, saying, Come, let us look one another in the face.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:8",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jehoash the king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, The thistle that was in Lebanon sent to the cedar that was in Lebanon, saying, Give thy daughter to my son to wife: and there passed by a wild beast that was in Lebanon, and trode down the thistle.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 90
          },
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 128
          },
          {
            "start": 224,
            "end": 227
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:9",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou hast indeed smitten Edom, and thine heart hath lifted thee up: glory of this, and tarry at home: for why shouldest thou meddle to thy hurt, that thou shouldest fall, even thou, and Judah with thee?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "Deut. 8:14; Jacob 2:13; Alma 1:32; 31:25; Morm. 8:28."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 82
          },
          {
            "start": 135,
            "end": 138
          },
          {
            "start": 171,
            "end": 175
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Deut. 8:14; Jacob 2:13; Alma 1:32; 31:25; Morm. 8:28.",
            "prettyString": "Deuteronomy 8:14; Jacob 2:13; Alma 1:32; 31:25; Mormon 8:28",
