        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:10",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "But Amaziah would not hear. Therefore Jehoash king of Israel went up; and he and Amaziah king of Judah looked one another in the face at Beth-shemesh, which belongeth to Judah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 157,
            "end": 166
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:11",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And Judah was put to the worse before Israel; and they fled every man to their tents.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:12",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jehoash king of Israel took Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Jehoash the son of Ahaziah, at Beth-shemesh, and came to Jerusalem, and brake down the wall of Jerusalem from the gate of Ephraim unto the corner gate, four hundred cubits.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:13",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And he took all the gold and silver, and all the vessels that were found in the house of the Lord, and in the treasures of the king’s house, and hostages, and returned to Samaria.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:14",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Now the rest of the acts of Jehoash which he did, and his might, and how he fought with Amaziah king of Judah, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 114
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:15",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jehoash slept with his fathers, and was buried in Samaria with the kings of Israel; and Jeroboam his son reigned in his stead.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:16",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah lived after the death of Jehoash son of Jehoahaz king of Israel fifteen years.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:17",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And the rest of the acts of Amaziah, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:18",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Now they made a conspiracy against him in Jerusalem: and he fled to Lachish; but they sent after him to Lachish, and slew him there.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:19",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And they brought him on horses: and he was buried at Jerusalem with his fathers in the city of David.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:20",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And all the people of Judah took Azariah, which was sixteen years old, and made him king instead of his father Amaziah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:21",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "He built Elath, and restored it to Judah, after that the king slept with his fathers.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 9:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Kgs. 9:26.",
            "prettyString": "1 Kings 9:26",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1kings",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 9,
                    "end": 9,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 26,
                        "end": 26
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:22",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "In the fifteenth year of Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah Jeroboam the son of Joash king of Israel began to reign in Samaria, and reigned forty and one years.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 143
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:23",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "And he did that which was evil in the sight of the Lord: he departed not from all the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 102,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 14:16; 2 Kgs. 10:29; 13:2 (1–2, 11); 15:9 (9, 18, 24)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 25
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 14:24",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "He restored the coast of Israel from the entering of Hamath unto the sea of the plain, according to the word of the Lord God of Israel, which he spake by the hand of his servant Jonah, the son of Amittai, the prophet, which was of Gath-hepher.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 178,
            "end": 183,
            "text": "Jonah 1:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 224,
            "end": 227
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jonah 1:1.",
            "prettyString": "Jonah 1:1",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jonah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
